1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:04,600
[Train wheels strike pairs of joints in the rails.]

2
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:13,815
On my way uptown, I count the doors.

3
00:00:16,030 --> 00:00:18,691
The window keeps my face for a while.

4
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:25,057
I can tell how late I am by the roofs.

5
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:32,915
At the coffee cart, I watch the light across the street.

6
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,300
[Traffic rises. A faint double tap.]

7
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:39,900
When it changes, I go.

8
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:46,917
At the top of the steps, the brass door is open.

9
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:53,400
Lucky, I think.

10
00:00:57,930 --> 00:01:01,338
In my notebook the whole trip fits on one line.

11
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:06,400
Brooklyn. Then class.

12
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,200
[Rail wheels, again.]

13
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:18,954
What did I put in the space between those words?

14
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:28,442
Same corner. Same light.

15
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,500
[Two light taps, now clear.]

16
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:38,400
There it is again.

17
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:45,847
A spoon touches the rim. Twice.

18
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,400
[A spoon rings twice against a cup.]

19
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:54,869
There's another cup behind the one I took.

20
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:02,639
The door hangs open for the length of a breath.

21
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:12,054
Someone's hand is still on the other side.

22
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:22,523
I remember the brass. I don't remember the hand.

23
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,600
[A door hinge. A soft click.]

24
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:32,198
If you ask how long it takes to get here,

25
00:02:35,130 --> 00:02:37,600
give me a minute.

26
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,000
[Two taps in the distance.]
